The three arcs are parts of circles of radius equal to the side of the equilateral triangle.  
Since the horizontal base of the figure is 2, the side length of the equilateral triangle is  

\[
s=2 .
\]

For each side we draw a circular sector of radius \(s\) and central angle \(60^{\circ}= \pi/3\).  
The area of one such sector is  

\[
\text{Area of sector}= \frac12 s^{2}\left(\frac{\pi}{3}\right)=\frac12\cdot 4\cdot\frac{\pi}{3}= \frac{2\pi}{3}.
\]

There are three congruent sectors, so the total area of the three sectors is  

\[
3\cdot\frac{2\pi}{3}=2\pi .
\]

The three sectors overlap in the central equilateral triangle.  
The area of that triangle is  

\[
\text{Area of triangle}= \frac{\sqrt3}{4}s^{2}= \frac{\sqrt3}{4}\cdot4 = \sqrt3 .
\]

Each point of the triangle is counted three times in the sum of the sector areas, so we must subtract the extra two copies of the triangle:

\[
\text{Area of trefoil}= 2\pi - 2\bigl(\text{area of triangle}\bigr)
= 2\pi - 2\sqrt3 .
\]

Hence the area of the trefoil whose horizontal base has length \(2\) is  

\[
\boxed{2\pi-2\sqrt3}.
\]<|im_end|>

