The two interior lines \(AE\) and \(AF\) trisect \(\angle BAD\), so  

\[
\angle BAD = 3x,\qquad 
\angle BAF = \angle FAD = x .
\]

Likewise, the same two lines trisect \(\angle CDA\), giving  

\[
\angle CDA = 3y,\qquad 
\angle CDF = \angle FDA = y .
\]

Hence in \(\triangle AFD\)

\[
\angle FAD = x,\qquad 
\angle ADF = y,
\]

so the remaining angle is  

\[
\angle AFD = 180^\circ-(x+y).
\]

The interior angles of quadrilateral \(ABCD\) satisfy  

\[
\angle A+\angle B+\angle C+\angle D = 360^\circ .
\]

Given \(\angle B =110^\circ\) and \(\angle C =100^\circ\),

\[
\angle A+\angle D = 360^\circ- (110^\circ+100^\circ)=150^\circ .
\]

But \(\angle A = 3x\) and \(\angle D = 3y\), so  

\[
3x+3y =150^\circ \Longrightarrow x+y = 50^\circ .
\]

Therefore  

\[
\angle AFD = 180^\circ-(x+y)=180^\circ-50^\circ =130^\circ .
\]

\[
\boxed{130}
\]<|im_end|>

